early also the  tip consumption so  the tip consumption is of course lower  in comparison to the magnetic bead base  kit  on the other hand the magnetic bead base  kit has a lower that volume or a lower  illusion volume  so in comparison to the silicon membrane  kit so you can see in the end  it's not that one technology is superior  about the other  it's more what is your key application  and what are you looking for  which you have to consider for your  optimal  choosing and choosing the optimal  technology in the end  just if you're interested in to dig  deeper into specific applications  eppendorf and mn together have recently  published  a series of application notes targeting  distinct applications for example dna  extraction from ffpe samples rna  extraction or on the smaller platform  for the 5073 isolated viral rna dna  isolation from medical samples  dna isolation from tissue samples or dna  deletion from blood samples  so these application nodes are all  available  on the home pages and please of course  feel free  if you have any questions to come  to ask them in the end of the session or  to  contact us separately in the next part i  just wanted to focus briefly  about three exemplary projects and  applications  eppendorf and mm have done together  in the past the first project is a  medical research project  on the 5073 platform so on the smaller  platform for a lower throughput  with 24 samples per run the main  application of this lab was to  to isolate viral and dna and rna  swap samples and then in the next step  subsequently  subject subject them to qpcr or qrt pcr  so basically the the main task the first  step of the workflow was the nucleic  acid purification using a kit of  macronutrient in this case the nuclear  micropathogen kit and then  in the second step also on the same  instrument the qpcr setup was also  set up so this shows that the  instruments  are not only for nuclear asset  purification but they can also use for  other applications showing the  versatility of these methods  of these systems um  the next project i wanted to briefly  describe is also a medical research  project about cancer profiling  the main application was dna extraction  from ffbe samples  those of you know or who are working  with ffbe samples know how tedious  these sample preparation can be  honestly i have to say this was one of  the most complex  nucleic acid purification workflows we  have established  on automation platforms so far  the reason for this is that with fpe  samples you first have to de-paraffinize  the sample then you have to decross link  and then  you can start with the lysis and  subsequently with the nucleic acid  extraction  so you have a lot of pre-treatment steps  which are usually  done manually and our aim was to  automate these these steps as good as we  can and in the end we had a hands-free  departurization and purification  purification workflow with a maximum  degree of automation  with only one manual intervention with  to a very distinct time point so  you can really put the glock on two  hours and you  walk to the system do some manual  pipetting three steps and that's it and  then you press start again so it was  really minimum of hands on time  and in the end what was really nice the  performance was equal to the manual  preparation  so in the end the customer was very  happy  that this tedious work and very time  consuming and also  time consuming and complicated work  could be now automated on the ep motion  systems  and coming to the last project one of my  favorite projects honestly i have to say  i i did with tim together a few years  ago  in the field of applied testings this  was a national institute  national forest institute in europe  and their aim was the investigation of  illegal wood shopping  so basically they were investigating  the um  they were checking the thermal waste as  well as the remains of cutted  trees in national parks and we're  comparing them  by dna sequencing so basically it's a  little bit like forest forensics or tree  forensics  and the main challenge of this was that  of course we had a kit the nuclear spin  96 plant kit for this purpose  but as you can imagine wood or sawmill  waste is not the best sample type to  extract dna out of it so you have a very  hard sample type and you have a very low  amount  of dna so and  additionally this institute also wanted  to check for fighter pathogens  so in the end they had a lot of  different applications and in the end we  had to do  some adaptations on the method on the  system  but now it's running freely so although  if the kit doesn't say this is  specifically for this  sample material or this application  there's always  something that r d can check if we can  make your application happy  happen in the end and with that i wanted  to  come to the next topic which will be a  little bit  tips and tricks for automated nucleic  acid purification so the session before  was more specific to my  negative kids and now it's a more  general  recommendation if you are going for  automation for nuclear acid purification  so we speak tim already spoke a little  bit about it  so what points to consider for  automation of course there are very  a lot of different points one should  consider before automating  um there are the main points from a  technic birth perspective  is always what is your throughput so do  you have a higher throughput a medium or  low throughput  and of course what are your application  requirements maybe you don't only want  to automate  nuclear asset purification but you also  want to automate other workflows maybe  you want to do limiting dilutions or  sample dilutions on the platform  maybe you can do the qpcr setup or ngs  workflows on the platform  so the versatility of of the platform  this is something you should always  consider  if you're going into the automation and  of course the next part  it's always the budget which is one key  factor  if you go going for automation and then  in the other part is the technology so  do you want to use magnetic beats do you  want to use silica membrane  so and of course does the performance  meet in the end with your expectations  another point which i highlighted here  is the service and support point  which you should consider already in the  beginning and this is not  meaning the service and support from  from like eppendorf or mahoney  it's more into who is using in the end  uh the platform so especially in  universities you buy a platform maybe  the phd student leaves after three years  because he has finished  so how how can the next person easily  work with these platforms so the ease of  use for  platforms for automation platforms such  as the promotion system  is of course a big key factor one should  consider  so now i have two examples of the most  common troubleshootings we see from the  r d side or from the application side  quite often in nuclear ethic  purification kits  so the one first example is the  inhibition of downstream analytics due  to wash buffer carryover  so basically the symptom is a qpcr or  pcr inhibition  and the reason for that is in 90 of the  cases that you have a  carryover of the wash buffer of ethanol  into the elevate and the end  and this ethanol inhibits then the  downstream analytics  so the symptom is always qpcr inhibition  and you can diagnose it very easily if  you check the residual volume  after each aspiration step on the  platform and  to do the volume which should be  left in the plate should be less than  five to ten microliters  so of course if it's zero microliters  that is very optimal  but in the normal under normal  conditions it's something between five  to ten micrometers  you can easily check this by stopping  the instrument  after the aspiration of the supernatant  taking out the plate  measuring it by a pipetting and then  thereby you can see  if the aspiration is efficient as you  want it to be  if you see that the residual volume is  higher than this amount  then you can start with the  troubleshooting so the first part would  be adjust the aspiration height by  surface teaching this is a very simplest  task which can be done by yourself on  the ep motion systems  if this does not help or only helps a  little bit then you can increase the  aspiration volume so  if you if you have aspirated before 600  microliters  you then aspirate 650 microliters  and of course of the third solution you  can prolong the drying step  to evaporate the remain residual ethanol  so these  three tips should always help you in  combination or  as a single a single task  to increase your or your got rid of your  qpcr inhibition or to increase your  performance  and one of the other most common  troubleshooting parts  especially with the magnetic beats is  the low purity  or low you have low purity due to  insufficient  resuspension of the magnetic beads  during magnetic bead-based processing  the resuspension  of the magnetic beads in the complete  wash buffer is really  the key to the for good performance  if the beats stay at the bottom during  mixing or shaking  then the performance will also be not  optimal  you can really you can easily see this  because the plates are more or less  transparent so you have a good  resuspension  when the plate comes off from the  thermal shaker and you can see the  the beads are distributed evenly in the  liquid  so that's a very good sign for a good  resuspension  we have a battery suspension if the  beads concentrate at the bottom and the  supernatant of the buffers  is still clear so then the shaking was  not enough  how to how to tackle then these these  symptoms is first of course you can  increase the shaking speed  be careful do not increase it too much  because otherwise  you risk spilling the buffers  by the shaking another point is you can  alternate the directions  so you can change between clockwise and  counter-clockwise like in an interval of  one minute or so  this helps to to loosen the bead pallet  the other part is what we always  recommend  is if you aspirate the supernatant after  you can see it in the picture so you  have the magnetic separation in the  middle you have the  removal of the supernatant and then you  add the washing buffer  and then you put it on the shaker you  can alter the order or the  um yeah the order of these steps  basically you aspirate the supernatant  and then you  place the empty plate on the shaker  shake it a little bit like 30 seconds  then move it back or and then add the  wash buffer  thereby because you shake the beads  without any buffer  you're already losing loosening up the  bead pellet and this helps then  with a complete resuspension and of  course if  nothing of these helps you can still  implement a pipette mixing step  i've as a closing remark i just want to  say usually  the mixing efficiency is very dependent  on the orbit of the shaker  so if you have a shaker with a good  orbit with a high  orbit then you don't run into into these  problems  okay and with these with this i wanted  to come to an end  and would like to hand over to my  colleague milan  thank you andreas for this very valuable  hands-on experience i think this is very  valuable information for the audience  because  uh it comes really from the application  r  d side and thank you also tim for  explaining uh the advantages of  automation  in general and of the ep motion  platforms  in particular um we are now at the end  of our presentation  we hope that this presentation was  useful  for you as our audience we will take  questions  uh from you we have time for a couple of  questions we  will not be able to answer all the  questions i think  and um yeah i just wanted already to say  thank you to  um to all of you for your attention  thank you gentlemen for your informative  presentation  let's jump right into that live q a  portion of our webinar  now we have so many questions that have  